 "lead": 2,
 "script": [
  {
   "beat": "hook",
   "text": "Nineteen thirty-two. The Australian army goes to war."
  },
  {
   "beat": "hook",
   "text": "The enemy? Twenty thousand emus."
  },
  {
   "beat": "hook",
   "text": "Machine guns. Ten thousand bullets."
  },
  {
   "beat": "hook",
   "text": "And the birds won."
  },
  {
   "beat": "host",
   "text": "This is the Great Emu War. Yes, really."
  },
  {
   "beat": "setup",
   "text": "Emus were eating the wheat farms of Western Australia, so the farmers asked for soldiers."
  },
  {
   "beat": "setup",
   "text": "Major Meredith arrived with two machine guns."
  },
  {
   "beat": "twist",
   "text": "But the emus split into tiny groups and ran, at fifty kilometres an hour."
  },
  {
   "beat": "twist",
   "text": "One gun jammed. The trucks couldn't keep up."
  },
  {
   "beat": "fact",
   "text": "After a month, he reported nine hundred and eighty-six kills, with nearly ten thousand bullets."
  },
  {
   "beat": "fact",
   "text": "That's ten bullets per bird. That's real."
  },
  {
   "beat": "end",
   "text": "The army pulled out. The emus kept the farms. Follow for more strange history."
  }
 ],
 "science": [
  {
   "claim": "Nov-Dec 1932, Western Australia; about 20,000 emus; Major G.P.W. Meredith with two Lewis guns and 10,000 rounds; a gun jammed; a truck-mounted gun could not keep up; emus split into small groups; he reported 986 kills with 9,860 rounds; little effect on the emu population.",
